1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,320
Welcome to Night 3 of the Cognitive Shutdown Method.

2
00:00:04,270 --> 00:00:11,182
Tonight we focus on the fuel, what you put into your body during the day, and how it shapes the night.

3
00:00:11,182 --> 00:00:13,991
Three substances matter the most.

4
00:00:13,991 --> 00:00:18,844
Caffeine has a half life of five to six hours in most adults.

5
00:00:18,844 --> 00:00:25,947
That means coffee at 2 PM still leaves half its dose circulating in your bloodstream at 8 PM.

6
00:00:25,947 --> 00:00:32,049
For sensitive people, that single dose can fragment sleep for the entire night.

7
00:00:32,049 --> 00:00:34,564
Alcohol is more deceptive.

8
00:00:34,564 --> 00:00:41,991
It helps you fall asleep faster, but it suppresses REM sleep and fragments the second half of the night.

9
00:00:41,991 --> 00:00:49,138
You wake at three AM, dehydrated, with the alcohol metabolites pulling you out of deep sleep.

10
00:00:49,138 --> 00:00:55,579
The drink that felt relaxing at 9 PM is the same drink waking you at 3 AM.

11
00:00:55,579 --> 00:01:02,329
Heavy meals close to bedtime force your digestive system to stay active when it should be powering down.

12
00:01:02,329 --> 00:01:07,358
The body cannot enter restorative sleep while it is still digesting.

13
00:01:07,358 --> 00:01:09,991
So the rules for tonight are simple.

14
00:01:09,991 --> 00:01:12,594
No caffeine after 2 PM.

15
00:01:12,594 --> 00:01:15,785
No alcohol within three hours of bed.

16
00:01:15,785 --> 00:01:19,564
Last meal at least two hours before lying down.

17
00:01:19,564 --> 00:01:25,623
And drink most of your water in the first half of the day so your bladder does not wake you up.

18
00:01:25,623 --> 00:01:27,873
Now, let your body settle.

19
00:01:27,873 --> 00:01:29,402
Loosen your jaw.

20
00:01:29,402 --> 00:01:32,667
Let your tongue rest behind your lower teeth.

21
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:35,844
Let your shoulders fall away from your ears.

22
00:01:35,844 --> 00:01:39,049
Breathe in through your nose for four seconds.

23
00:01:39,049 --> 00:01:41,182
Hold for seven seconds.

24
00:01:41,182 --> 00:01:44,902
Release slowly through your mouth for eight seconds.

25
00:01:44,902 --> 00:01:46,079
Again.

26
00:01:46,079 --> 00:01:47,549
In for four.

27
00:01:47,549 --> 00:01:49,152
Hold for seven.

28
00:01:49,152 --> 00:01:50,520
Out for eight.

29
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:51,829
Once more.

30
00:01:51,829 --> 00:01:53,299
In for four.

31
00:01:53,299 --> 00:01:54,902
Hold for seven.

32
00:01:54,902 --> 00:01:56,270
Out for eight.

33
00:01:56,270 --> 00:01:58,755
Your body has what it needs to rest.

34
00:01:58,755 --> 00:02:00,094
Sleep well.

